{{Documentation/Header}}
Returns a value depending on whether the current page is a documentation subpage. Used inside other templates to suppress categories, notices or demos when they are being shown on a <code>/doc</code> page rather than in real use.

Also returns true for a translation subpage of a doc page (e.g. <code>/doc/de</code>) when the Translate extension is active.

==Syntax==
{{T|IsDocSubpage|block=1
|v1=override =
|v2=true =
|v3=false =
}}

==Usage==
<pre>{{#if:{{IsDocSubpage}}|shown only on /doc|shown everywhere else}}</pre>

{| class="dataTable sortable"
! Parameter !! Aliases !! Label !! Description !! Type !! Default !! Status
|-
| <code>override</code> || – || Subpage name || The subpage name to test for instead of <code>doc</code>. || string || doc ||
|-
| <code>true</code> || – || True value || Returned when the page '''is''' a doc subpage. || string || 1 ||
|-
| <code>false</code> || – || False value || Returned when the page is '''not''' a doc subpage. || string || ''(empty)'' ||
|}